SUMMARY:The Tragedy of Hamlet: Prince of Denmark
DESCRIPTION:Following a successful worldwide run after its original debut in Toronto\, this acclaimed dance-theatre collaboration between director Robert Lepage and choreographer Guillaume Côté returns to where it all began for performances this April. \nExperience Emotion in Motion\, where every gesture\, every leap\, and every pause is meticulously crafted to convey the deepest human emotions. Dive into Visual Spectacle where Innovative set designs and ethereal lighting create a surreal atmosphere that blurs the lines between reality and the subconscious. An original score accompanies the performance\, intensifying the emotional impact and drawing you deeper into the narrative.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/the-tragedy-of-hamlet-prince-of-denmark-2/
LOCATION:The Elgin & Winter Garden Theatres\, The Elgin & Winter Garden Theatres\, 189 Yonge St.\, M5B1M4 Toronto\, Ontario\, Canada\, Toronto\, M5B 1M4
CATEGORIES:Dance,Performing Arts,Theatre & Opera
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/the-tragedy-of-hamlet-prince-of-denmark.png
END:VEVENT
